.vercel

# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit env files. The one historical exception is .env.local, which is
# already tracked and holds ONLY public values (VITE_* vars are compiled into
# the client bundle by design, and the Supabase anon key is public — the
# database is protected by Row Level Security, not by hiding this key).
# Removing it from git requires first setting VITE_SUPABASE_URL and
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY in the Vercel project's Environment Variables,
# otherwise the production build ships an undefined Supabase config.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.production
.env.development
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
service-account*.json

# ─── Build output & deps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.cache/

# ─── System / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
